{
  "_comment": [
    "Photographic material art generated through the Higgsfield MCP.",
    "",
    "Each entry maps one atlas tile (the names come from TILE in",
    "src/gfx/textures.js) to a completed Higgsfield image job. The palettes",
    "handed to the generator are the same hexes the procedural painter uses,",
    "so the generated art lands in the same colour space as the fallback and",
    "the two can be swapped without relighting anything.",
    "",
    "`npm run bake-art` downloads these, makes them genuinely seamless,",
    "pulls their mean luminance towards the procedural tile they replace, and",
    "composites them into the atlas layout. Tiles not listed here stay",
    "procedural — window grids, signage and lamp lenses are structure, not",
    "material, and a photograph is the wrong tool for them.",
    "",
    "`match` is how hard to pull the generated tile's luminance towards the",
    "procedural one: 0 keeps the photograph as generated, 1 matches exactly."
  ],
